},"3614":{"id":"/learn-11","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"Reading later operate pages without tripping on jargon"},"3615":{"id":"/learn-12","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"Not treating ez-comfy-stack occupancy rules as this cluster's capacity gate"},"3616":{"id":"/learn-13","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-lab","content":"This is **not** a ComfyUI beginner course. Still images and video on one Spark with Docker Compose: ez-comfy-stack."},"3617":{"id":"/learn-14","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#k3s-on-spark","content":"Each GB10 node is one GPU, 20 Arm cores, 128 GB unified memory. Kubelet reservations and Resource Guard keep SSH and K3s alive while Jobs request most of the rest."},"3618":{"id":"/learn-15","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#k3s-on-spark","content":"spark0 runs the K3s **server** and a **worker**"},"3619":{"id":"/learn-16","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#k3s-on-spark","content":"spark1+ are agents"},"3620":{"id":"/learn-17","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#k3s-on-spark","content":"GPU Operator installs drivers, device plugin, DCGM"},"3621":{"id":"/learn-18","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#k3s-on-spark","content":"Bootstrap is Ansible. Day-2 mutations go through `manage.sh` (`bazelisk run //:manage -- …`) so confirmations and capacity checks stay in one place."},"3622":{"id":"/learn-19","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","safety","k3s","nccl","resources"],"type":"text","url":"/