up_vars`\nuse for `k3s_control_plane`. Inventory: generated from `ansible/inventory/lab.yaml`\n(legacy hand-made example: `ansible/inventory/hosts.ini.example`)."],[49,"The output is at `docs/generated/shell/reference.md` and appears in the site under **Reference > Code-Generated Reference**."],[782,"The playbook installs prereqs, highspeed netplan on 2+ nodes (from the generated per-node\nnetplan when present), K3s server on the **orchestrator** node (`role: orchestrator` in\n`lab.yaml`), agents, labels, kubeconfig."],[95,"The previous short paragraph has been replaced by this more complete description."],[1277,"The proxy must stay up if backends are down (per-model 503 is fine)."],[3095,"The rule"],[3109,"The rule this repository holds itself to, and why it is a safety rule here"],[225,"The Shell Commands & Helpers page is **not** written by hand. It is produced from structured comments inside the scripts."],[3574,"The switch block (host, read-only user, `port_map`) lives in `lab.yaml`; the password is\n`LAB_SWITCH_PASSWORD` in the operator's environment only. Qwen 3.5 397B NVFP4 is the\ncanonical TP=4 Job here. Cabling and port map: Choose topology."],[3568,"The switch fabric is a managed 4× 400G QSFP-DD device; each node sees **one** RoCE link:"],[4604,"The switch is a managed 4-port 400G QSFP-DD device with a 10GbE management port:"],[4608,"The switch's management IP (e.g. `10.0.0.2`) is declared in the `switch:` block; only a\n**read-only** API probe may use it. The switch password is read from the\n`LAB_SWITCH_PASSWORD` environment variable at runtime — never commit it."],[32,"The traditional Makefile and direct `ansible-playbook` / `bazelisk run //:manage --` invocations remain available for compatibility and for people who have not installed bazelisk."],[3155,"The type, the runtime allowlist, and the parser cannot drift apart, which is how `InferenceModelName` and `NemotronStackId` used to work: each was a hand-listed union mirroring a hand-listed `z.enum([